1597	1787	1588	1588	He	6	“ I can tell yuh the kinda cow - puncher he is ; I 've saw 'em workin ' at it . Haw - haw - haw ! They 'll start out to move ten or a dozen head uh tame old cows from one field to another , and there 'll be six or eight fellers , rigged up like this here tray - spot , ridin ' along , important as hell , drivin ' them few cows down a lane , with peach trees on both sides , by cripes , jingling their big , silver spurs , all wearin ' fancy chaps to ride four or five miles down the road . Honest to grandma , they call that punchin ' cows ! Oh , he 's a Native Son , all right . I 've saw lots of 'em , only I never saw one so far away from the Promised Land before . That there looks queer to me . Natiff Sons -- the real ones , like him -- are as scarce outside Calyforny as buffalo are right here in this coulee . ”
